/**
 * @file aria
 * @author jung-kwang lee (ntoskrnl7@gmail.com)
 * @brief ARIA block cipher (RFC 5794 / KS X 1213-1)
 *
 * Follows the specification designed by KISA and published as RFC 5794. It is
 * an involutional SPN, so encryption and decryption take the same path and
 * only the round keys are exchanged.
 *
 * On how the S-boxes are handled: RFC 5794 defines all four S-boxes as lookup
 * tables only and does not give the algebraic definition, that is the inverse
 * in GF(2^8) followed by an affine transformation. Copying tables into the
 * source was therefore kept to a minimum.
 *   - SB1 is the same as the AES S-box, so it is generated from the algebraic
 *     definition (ctl/detail/sbox)
 *   - SB3 is the inverse of SB1, so it is derived
 *   - SB2 exists in the specification only as a table, so it is transcribed
 *     from the document (sb2_table in this file)
 *   - SB4 is the inverse of SB2, so it is derived
 * The transcribed SB2 is checked at compile time for being a permutation, so a
 * single mistyped byte makes compilation fail.
 *
 * @version 0.1
 *
 * @copyright Copyright (c) 2022 C++ Cryptographics template library Authors
 *
 */
